# Testing Patterns

## Testing Framework
- **E2E Testing**: Playwright for end-to-end tests
- **Test Location**: `tests/` directory
- **Test Commands**: Defined in package.json

## Test Commands
- `npm run test:e2e` - Run all E2E tests
- `npm run test:e2e:ui` - Run tests with UI
- `npm run test:e2e:headed` - Run tests in headed mode
- `npm run test:e2e:debug` - Debug tests
- `npm run test:report` - Generate test report
- `npm run test:chromium` - Run on Chromium
- `npm run test:firefox` - Run on Firefox
- `npm run test:webkit` - Run on WebKit
- `npm run test:mobile` - Run on mobile Chrome

## Test Categories
- **Form Validation**: `test:validation` - Form validation tests
- **Conditional Logic**: `test:conditional` - Conditional form logic
- **Submission Status**: `test:submission` - Form submission tests
- **Auto Save**: `test:autosave` - Auto-save functionality

## Testing Best Practices
- Test authentication flows
- Test role-based access control
- Test form validation
- Test API integration
- Test responsive design
- Test dark mode functionality

## Test Structure
- Organize tests by feature
- Use descriptive test names
- Group related tests
- Use proper setup/teardown
- Clean up after tests

## E2E Test Patterns
```typescript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('should login with valid credentials', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.fill('[name="uniqueId"]', 'SUPER001');
  await page.fill('[name="password"]', 'super123');
  await page.click('button[type="submit"]');
  await expect(page).toHaveURL('/super-admin/dashboard');
});
```

## Test Data
- Use test fixtures for consistent data
- Mock API responses when needed
- Use test users for authentication
- Clean up test data after tests

## Accessibility Testing
- Test keyboard navigation
- Test screen reader compatibility
- Test color contrast
- Test ARIA attributes

## Performance Testing
- Test page load times
- Test API response times
- Test large data sets
- Test concurrent operations
